{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxqgyF885rwagWdtyKLL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four steps are done, and I read the rule back after enabling it. It shows as enabled.\n\n- **Data view:** \"Kibana Sample Data Logs\" uses `timestamp` as its time field.\n- **Dashboard:** \"S4-6a43fcfd Web logs\" has two panels. One is \"Requests over time\" and the other is the response-code panel.\n- **Alert rule:** \"S4-6a43fcfd 5xx errors\" runs every minute. It fires when more than 10 requests with a response code from 500 to 599 arrive within 5 minutes. It was created disabled, so I enabled it. Its status reads \"ok\".\n- **Panel edit:** The response-code panel is now titled \"Responses by code\". The dashboard read-back confirms the new title.\n\nThe rule matches codes with a text range from \"500\" to \"599\" on `response.keyword`, because `response` is stored as a string. That covers every three-digit code in that span. I didn't run the query against the data, so I haven't confirmed how many requests it matches.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":533,"cache_read_input_tokens":20859,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":533},"output_tokens":357,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0da1e72d-e9d9-58d9-b388-fca8d0eba393","uuid":"b841c96e-329b-4fa8-98ea-d45c41b9aacd","timestamp":"2026-10-12T18:46:38.996Z","request_id":"req_011Cfxqgy1yfZi7hCUpVWCin"}
